# FRONTEND TDD — RED PHASE SKILL

## Goal
Define exactly one user-visible behavior by writing a single failing frontend test.

---

## Input
- A clear UI behavior described from the user's perspective

---

## Output
- Exactly one failing test
- No production code

---

## Core Principle

Frontend tests validate **what the user sees and does**, not internal implementation.

---

## Rules

- Write test code only
- Do NOT write components, hooks, or services
- Do NOT refactor anything
- Do NOT modify existing tests
- Exactly ONE test must be written
- Test MUST fail

---

## Behavior Rule (STRICT)

The test MUST describe:

- What the user sees (rendered output)
- OR what the user does (interaction)
- OR how the UI responds

❌ Forbidden:
- Testing internal state
- Testing implementation details
- Testing hooks directly
- Testing service logic

---

## Architecture Alignment

The test MUST respect frontend architecture:

- Services MUST be mocked
- No real API calls allowed
- UI must be tested through components only
- Data must come through state or props (never directly from API)

---

## Test Structure (MANDATORY BDD FORMAT)

All tests MUST follow explicit Given / When / Then structure:

```ts
// GIVEN: initial UI state or mocked service response
// WHEN: user interaction or render occurs
// THEN: expected UI output or behavior